statement:
Let $p$ and $q$ be distinct primes between $4$ and $18$, and suppose $pq=t+p+q$. For real $x$, show that
\[
\left(x-\binom{(p-1)(q-1)}{p-1}\right)^2+\binom{(p-1)(q-1)}{p-1}
=\binom{(p-1)(q-1)-1}{p-1}+\binom{(p-1)(q-1)-1}{p-2}
\]
if and only if $x=\binom{(p-1)(q-1)}{p-1}$.
